   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the family court act and a chapter of the laws of 2020\namending the family court act, relating to the placement of a former foster\ncare youth during a certain state of emergency, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S.8834 and A.10581-B, in relation to placement without a motion\nand motions being heard and determined on an expedited basis and in relation\nto the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S2075",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2075-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1055 & 1091, Fam Ct Act; amd §3, Chap of 2020 (as proposed in S.8834 & A. 10581-B)",
    "lawSection": "Family Court Act",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2075\n\nSPONSOR: BRISPORT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the family court act and a chapter of the laws of 2020\namending the family court act, relating to the placement of a former\nfoster care youth during a certain state of emergency, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S.8834 and A.10581-B, in relation to placement\nwithout a motion and motions being heard and determined on an expedited\nbasis and in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.\n2020, c. 346.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by providing that a\nformer foster care youth may re-enter the foster care system during the\nstate of emergency declared pursuant to executive order 202 of 2020, or\nany extension or subsequent executive order issued in response to the\nnovel coronavirus (COVID-19) pandemic. It also clarifies that nothing in\nthis legislation shall prohibit a local social service district from\nfiling a motion for requisite findings needed to claim reimbursement\nunder Title IV-E of the Federal Social Security Act to support the\nyouth's care, and the family court shall hear and determine such\nmotions.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 50 of 2020, the Executive supports the goals\nof this legislation, yet noted the need for technical changes so as to\nnot jeopardize federal funding. This chapter amendment reflects agreed-\nupon changes by the Executive and the Legislature to fix these issues.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 346 of the Laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
